    "hypothesis": "A balanced contiguous OpenMP partition of the flattened point set, combined with per-thread max-heaps and a deterministic merge, should remove shared updates and improve the scan cost from O(P*k) insertion work to O(P log k). It may help most when the point set and k are large enough to offset heap, sorting, and merge overhead.",
    "notes": "Only src/knn.c is changed; no experiment source IDs were supplied. The local candidate storage can reach O(P) when k is large, and each point incurs a group-offset search. No commands or measurements were run; the controller should evaluate correctness and performance.",
